{"name":"Light My Fire","hex":"#f8611a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light my fire","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To excite or arouse someone; to turn someone on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light_my_fire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Light My Fire","blocks":[{"text":"\"Light My Fire\" is a song by the American rock band the Doors. Although it was principally written by the band's guitarist, Robby Krieger, songwriting was credited to the entire band. Recognized as one of the earliest examples of psychedelic rock, it was recorded in 1966 and released in January 1967 on their eponymous debut album. Due to its erotic lyrics and innovative structure, the track is widely regarded as an anthem of the 1960s psychedelia and counterculture movements."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/76/Light_My_Fire.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light_My_Fire","wikidata":"Q580010"},{"title":"Light My Fire (Sean Paul song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Light My Fire\" is a song recorded by Jamaican singer Sean Paul featuring guest vocals from American singer Gwen Stefani and Jamaican dancehall artist Shenseea. He wrote \"Light My Fire\" with Shenseea, Saul Alexander \"AC\" Castillo Vasquez, Gamal Kosh Lewis, Allan Peter Grigg, Rosina Russell, and Emily Warren. It was produced by Grigg, AC, and Paul's brother Jason Jigzag Henriques. In interviews, Paul revealed the collaboration was a result of his admiration of both Stefani and Shenseea. It was digitally released as a single by Island Records on 25 May 2022 in support of Paul's eighth studio album, Scorcha (2022)."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light_My_Fire_(Sean_Paul_song)","wikidata":"Q115825190"},{"title":"My Fire","blocks":[{"text":"\"My Fire\" is a song recorded and performed by American dance musicians Nile Rodgers and Tony Moran, featuring vocals from American singer Kimberly Davis. The song is co-produced by Rodgers, Moran and Georg Bissen. The collaboration marks Rodgers' fifth, Moran's seventh, and Davis' first number one, on Billboard's Dance Club Songs chart, reaching the summit in its July 29, 2017 issue."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Fire","wikidata":"Q48772709"},{"title":"Fire","blocks":[{"text":"Fire is the rapid oxidation of a fuel in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.\nFlames, the most visible portion of the fire, are produced in the combustion reaction when the fuel reaches its ignition point temperature. Flames from hydrocarbon fuels consist primarily of carbon dioxide, water vapor, oxygen, and nitrogen. If hot enough, the gases may become ionized to produce plasma. The color and intensity of the flame depend on the type of fuel and composition of the surrounding gases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Large_bonfire.jpg/330px-Large_bonfire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire","wikidata":"Q3196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Voxcontinental.jpg/500px-Voxcontinental.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Voxcontinental.jpg/500px-Voxcontinental.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Vox Continental organ was played by Ray Manzarek for the song's recording","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVoxcontinental.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Light_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg/500px-Light_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Light_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg/1280px-Light_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Light_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg/500px-Light_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cash Box advertisement, May 27, 1967","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALight_My_Fire_-_ad_1967.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dc/Light_My_Fire_-_Jos%C3%A9_Feliciano.jpeg/250px-Light_My_Fire_-_Jos%C3%A9_Feliciano.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/dc/Light_My_Fire_-_Jos%C3%A9_Feliciano.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dc/Light_My_Fire_-_Jos%C3%A9_Feliciano.jpeg/250px-Light_My_Fire_-_Jos%C3%A9_Feliciano.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALight_My_Fire_-_Jos%C3%A9_Feliciano.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Amii_Stewart-Light_My_Fire.jpg/250px-Amii_Stewart-Light_My_Fire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3a/Amii_Stewart-Light_My_Fire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3a/Amii_Stewart-Light_My_Fire.jpg/250px-Amii_Stewart-Light_My_Fire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmii_Stewart-Light_My_Fire.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/88/WY_LMF.jpg/330px-WY_LMF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/88/WY_LMF.jpg/